# Production environment for `next build` / `next start`.
#
# Next.js only reads this file when NODE_ENV is production, so `next dev` is
# unaffected and keeps falling back to http://localhost:3000 (see
# `lib/seo/site.ts`). There is no secret here — NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# compiled into the client bundle by definition — so this is committed rather
# than left for each deploy to rediscover.
#
# The scheme must match what Nginx actually serves. It is http today per
# `docs/operations/OPS-DEPLOYMENT.md`; declaring https while serving http would
# point every canonical tag and sitemap entry at a URL that does not answer,
# which keeps the site out of the index entirely rather than merely ranking it
# lower. When HTTPS goes live, change this line and set JC_COOKIE_SECURE=true
# in the backend env at the same time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://jc.sspacee.com
